      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I reported this bug around mid march through email. \n\nLets say you try to go back to your home world which is private and unpublished world but you get stuck in the loading screen loop. Now if a friend tries to join on you while you are stuck in the loading screen loop, it will send them to a public instance of that private unpublished world. That private instance that you were meant to load into was clearly never successfully created so when a friend tries to join you it errors out and sends them to the random public instance.\n\nThis should never happen.\n\nAs a note, the same thing will occur for example if you try to join someone in a public instance of a world that ends up being at capacity for player count. It sends you to a random public instance if it can not get you into the world. That seems fine, but private instances and or unpublished worlds should not load into public instances or at all.\n\nI like the suggestion by Waai to just send them to the home world. Maybe add a popup message explaining what happened \"Unable to join instance: <insert reason>\". example reasons could be, capacity full, instance does not exist, instance could not be found try again, etc",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
